+/// One whole number of seconds, as a duration, refusing zero and text that is not a number.
+///
+/// The zero is refused here rather than at the use site because there is no use for it: a lease of
+/// nothing expires under the worker that holds the row, and a drain of nothing refuses to let an
+/// attempt answer, so both are a deployment turning its own service off in a way it did not mean.
+fn read_seconds(
